 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "rtl-design-creation",
  "visit": 3,
  "text": "DONE. The synthesis failure was a wrong port name on `USR_ACCESSE2`, and I fixed it. I have only run lint, which passes. I did not run simulate or check, and I did not re-run the Vivado build.\n\n- **Cause:** the real `USR_ACCESSE2` primitive has a port called `DATAVALID`, but `rtl/freq_meter_top.sv` connected `DATA_VALID`. Vivado rejected that (Synth 8-11365), which is why `por_reset` and `freq_meter_top` both showed as failed to synthesise. `por_reset` itself was fine.\n- **Top fix:** `freq_meter_top.sv` now connects `.DATAVALID(usr_valid)`. I also changed `CEMASK` on `BUFG_GT` from a 3-bit value to the 1-bit `1'b0`, since I recalled the real primitive's `CEMASK` as 1 bit. I did not check that against the Vivado primitive.\n- **Stub fix:** `rtl/xilinx_sim_stubs.sv` now matches: the `USR_ACCESSE2` stand-in port is `DATAVALID`, and the `BUFG_GT` stand-in `CEMASK` is 1 bit."
 },
